cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "datasource-queen: durable state, SQLite on a VFS whose pages live in FoundationDB"
abstract: >
  Durable state, packed by what a caller can reach and what it cannot. The queen is
  the game and the store's caller, a plane with no networking; the planner plane is
  the Queen's one decision, as an HTN domain over the ward; and below both is SQLite
  over a VFS whose pages are FoundationDB transactions, so no client ever opens a
  database and authority never moves. CI plays two wards on two seeds against a live
  FoundationDB and holds them to their arithmetic, so the domain has a workload that
  runs on every push rather than a claim that it would.
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    email: ernest.lee@chibifire.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4570-1436"
version: 0.1.0-dev.1
date-released: "2026-08-17"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/datasource-queen"
keywords:
  - sqlite
  - foundationdb
  - htn-planning
  - durable-state
references:

  - type: software
    title: "FoundationDB"
    authors:
      - name: "Apple Inc. and the FoundationDB project authors"
    url: "https://github.com/apple/foundationdb"
    notes: >
      Every durable transaction, and the pages themselves. Below the planes rather than
      one of them. The fabric's pinned fork is datasource-foundationdb.

  - type: software
    title: "SQLite"
    authors:
      - name: "D. Richard Hipp and the SQLite developers"
    url: "https://sqlite.org/"
    notes: >
      The query surface, reached only through a custom VFS. What is borrowed is the
      language and the file format's page discipline; what is replaced is the file.

  - type: software
    title: "interactor-taskweft: the planner plane"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    url: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/interactor-taskweft"
    notes: "Vendored at thirdparty/taskweft. The HTN planner src/planner.cpp states its domain against."

  - type: software
    title: "contract-bus: the weft plane harness"
    authors:
      - family-names: Lee
        given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
    url: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/contract-bus"
    notes: "Vendored at thirdparty/, with the store-plane and gateway-edge members beside it."

  - type: software
    title: "versitygw: an S3-compatible gateway"
    url: "https://github.com/versity/versitygw"
    notes: "The endpoint fdbbackup writes to. Backup is a different durability question from the pages, and it is answered outside the cluster."
